name    mod-dungeon-challenge: a running run comes back after it left the server's memory
# Server-side test bot run (mod-fl-testbots), T1, Mythic+ idea 10. A run is a row of characters
# dungeon_challenge_active while it runs. `.dchallenge forget` drops it from memory and keeps the row - what a
# restart or an instance unload does to the run. Bot a then reconnects (`relog`, the core's logout and login in
# the same instance): entering the instance restores the run with its level, deaths and running clock. A real
# restart cannot be shown with bots: the test bot module takes its bots out of their instances at shutdown.
timeout 150s

bot a warrior
group party

place 727 13288.5 11776.2 -31.5
require a alive
as gm .dchallenge start 574 5
waitfor gm map 574 timeout 20s
waitfor a map 574 timeout 20s
wait 2s
as gm .dchallenge status
expect output has "level 5"
expect output lacks "(restored)"

log a death is saved with the run
do a die
wait 1s
do a revive
as gm .dchallenge status
expect output has "deaths 1"

log the run leaves memory, a participant comes back
as gm .dchallenge forget
expect output has "forgotten"
as gm .dchallenge status
expect output has "No Dungeon Challenge run"
wait 2s
do a relog
waitfor a exists timeout 20s
waitfor a map 574 timeout 20s
wait 2s
as gm .dchallenge status
expect output has "level 5"
expect output has "(restored)"
expect output has "deaths 1"

cleanup
place 727 13288.5 11776.2 -31.5
wait 2s
as gm .dchallenge status
expect output has "No Dungeon Challenge run"
